1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,120
The British called him the Desert Fox,

2
00:00:02,170 --> 00:00:05,930
but in the end it was not the enemy who killed him, it was his own regime.

3
00:00:05,950 --> 00:00:07,630
His name was Erwin Rommel.

4
00:00:07,650 --> 00:00:11,600
On 12 February 1941 he landed in Tripoli.

5
00:00:11,700 --> 00:00:14,760
He was meant to support the Italians in Libya and wait,

6
00:00:14,780 --> 00:00:18,910
but Rommel attacked and drove the British back to the Egyptian border.

7
00:00:18,930 --> 00:00:22,240
He led from the front, often from a small Fieseler Storch.

8
00:00:22,360 --> 00:00:25,270
Only Tobruk held out, for almost eight months.

9
00:00:25,310 --> 00:00:27,180
His enemies talked about him so often

10
00:00:27,200 --> 00:00:31,450
that the British commander-in-chief Claude Auchinleck wrote to his commanders

11
00:00:31,470 --> 00:00:35,100
to stop talking about Rommel and speak only of the Germans.

12
00:00:35,120 --> 00:00:40,960
In June 1942 Tobruk fell, and at 50 Rommel became a field marshal.

13
00:00:41,020 --> 00:00:44,020
A few months later he failed at El Alamein.

14
00:00:44,070 --> 00:00:48,090
Hitler ordered victory or death, Rommel retreated anyway.

15
00:00:48,110 --> 00:00:52,290
In 1944 he had millions of mines laid on the Atlantic Wall

16
00:00:52,310 --> 00:00:55,340
and stakes driven into the beaches, known as Rommel's asparagus.

17
00:00:55,360 --> 00:00:59,870
But after the Allied landings he considered the war lost and said so openly.

18
00:00:59,890 --> 00:01:04,460
After the assassination attempt of 20 July, his name came up in the interrogations of the conspirators.

19
00:01:04,480 --> 00:01:09,970
On 14 October 1944 two generals stopped outside his house in Herrlingen.

20
00:01:09,990 --> 00:01:13,510
They gave him a choice: the People's Court or poison.

21
00:01:13,530 --> 00:01:17,720
Rommel said goodbye to his wife and son and got into the car.

22
00:01:17,760 --> 00:01:19,300
Shortly afterwards he was dead.

23
00:01:19,320 --> 00:01:21,820
Officially, he died of his wounds.

24
00:01:21,840 --> 00:01:23,320
Hitler sent a wreath,

25
00:01:23,340 --> 00:01:29,320
and at the funeral in Ulm Field Marshal von Rundstedt said: His heart belonged to the Führer.

26
00:01:29,380 --> 00:01:33,500
The world only learned the truth after the war, from his son Manfred.
